{#
  The evidence pack. One self-contained document: inline styles, embedded
  photographs, an SVG diagram drawn from the case's own coordinates. Nothing
  here may reference an external URL — a pack is usually read offline, and a
  broken image is worse than no image. See pack.py for why this is HTML.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Evidence pack — {{ case.case_id }}</title>
<style>
  /* System fonts only. A web font would be an external request, and the local
     language block needs Indic shaping the browser already does with whatever
     the machine has installed. The stack names the Noto families first because
     they are the ones most likely to be present and to cover every script this
     project drafts in. */
  :root {
    --ink: #1e241f;
    --muted: #5c665e;
    --rule: #d5dcd6;
    --paper: #ffffff;
    --wash: #f4f6f4;
    --flag: #8a4b3c;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 28px 20px 64px;
    background: var(--wash);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Noto Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .sheet {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 40px 44px 52px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  h1 { font-size: 25px; margin: 0 0 4px; line-height: 1.2; }
  h2 {
    font-size: 15px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    margin: 34px 0 10px;
    padding-bottom: 5px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: system-ui, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  h3 { font-size: 14px; margin: 18px 0 6px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .subtitle { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 18px; font-size: 13px; }
  .status {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: system-ui, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    margin-right: 6px;
  }
  dl.facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 4px 18px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  dl.facts dt { color: var(--muted); }
  dl.facts dd { margin: 0; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; }
  .prose { white-space: pre-wrap; }
  .local {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    font-family: "Noto Sans Devanagari", "Noto Sans Kannada", "Noto Sans Tamil",
      "Noto Sans Telugu", "Noto Sans Bengali", "Noto Sans Gujarati",
      "Noto Sans Gurmukhi", "Noto Sans Malayalam", "Noto Sans Oriya",
      "Nirmala UI", "Lohit Devanagari", "Noto Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  figure { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--rule); display: block; }
  figcaption { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 5px; }
  .photos { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--flag);
    padding: 8px 0 8px 12px;
    margin: 12px 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; font-size: 13.5px; }
  .timeline li { padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--rule); }
  .timeline time { color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; margin-right: 10px; }
  footer { margin-top: 34px; padding-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
           font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .diagram { border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--wash); }

  @page { size: A4; margin: 15mm; }
  @media print {
    body { background: #fff; padding: 0; font-size: 11.5pt; }
    .sheet { border: 0; padding: 0; max-width: none; }
    /* Keep a photograph, a fact table and the diagram whole, but let a long
       section such as the complaint body flow across a page break. Holding a
       whole section together sounds tidier and prints half-empty pages. */
    figure, dl.facts, .diagram, .note { break-inside: avoid; }
    h2, h3 { break-after: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="sheet">

  <header>
    <h1>Pollution complaint — evidence pack</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Case {{ case.case_id }} &middot;
      compiled {{ generated_at.strftime("%d %B %Y, %H:%M UTC") }}
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="status">{{ case.status.value.replace("_", " ") }}</span>
      <span class="status">stage: {{ case.stage.value }}</span>
      {% if escalation_due %}<span class="status">escalation due</span>{% endif %}
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>At a glance</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Observed</dt><dd>{{ report.observed_at.strftime("%d %B %Y, %H:%M UTC") }}</dd>
      <dt>Location</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.address or "Address not resolved" }}
          ({{ "%.5f"|format(report.latitude) }}, {{ "%.5f"|format(report.longitude) }})</dd>
      {% if case.evidence %}
      <dt>Classified as</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.evidence.pollution_type.value.replace("_", " ") }},
          {{ case.evidence.severity }} severity,
          confidence {{ "%.2f"|format(case.evidence.confidence) }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Evidence basis</dt>
      <dd>
        {% if photographs|length == 0 %}
          No photograph; the citizen's written account
        {% elif photographs|length == 1 %}
          One photograph and the citizen's note
        {% else %}
          {{ photographs|length }} photographs of one event, and the citizen's note
        {% endif %}
      </dd>
      {% if case.jurisdiction %}
      <dt>Filed with</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.authority_name }}
          ({{ case.jurisdiction.authority_tier }})</dd>
      <dt>Under</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.statute }}{% if case.jurisdiction.section %},
          {{ case.jurisdiction.section }}{% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.filed_at %}
      <dt>Filed on</dt><dd>{{ case.filed_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.acknowledged_at %}
      <dt>Acknowledged</dt><dd>{{ case.acknowledged_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.escalated_at %}
      <dt>Escalated</dt><dd>{{ case.escalated_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.resolved_at %}
      <dt>Resolved</dt><dd>{{ case.resolved_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.withdrawn_at %}
      <dt>Withdrawn</dt><dd>{{ case.withdrawn_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if cluster %}
      <dt>Pattern</dt>
      <dd>{{ cluster.cluster_id }} &mdash; {{ cluster.report_count }} reports</dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Photographs</h2>
    {% if photographs %}
      <div class="photos">
        {% for photo in photographs %}
        <figure>
          <img src="{{ photo.src }}" alt="{{ photo.caption }}">
          <figcaption>{{ photo.caption }}</figcaption>
        </figure>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% if photographs|length > 1 %}
      <p class="subtitle">
        These are angles on one event, submitted together with one report.
      </p>
      {% endif %}
    {% else %}
      <p class="note">
        No photograph was submitted with this report{% if report.image_paths %},
        or the files are no longer on disk{% endif %}. The classification below rests on the
        citizen's written account, and the complaint is written as testimony rather than as
        photographic evidence.
      </p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if report.note %}
      <h3>The citizen's note</h3>
      <p class="prose">{{ report.note }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Location</h2>
    <div class="diagram">{{ map_svg|safe }}</div>
    <p class="subtitle">
      A diagram, not a map. It is drawn from the coordinates on the case, with no basemap
      or map tiles, so this document opens without making any network request.
      {%- if case.corroboration and case.corroboration.upwind_source_latitude is not none %}
      The open circle is where the wind at the time of the report says a source would have
      to lie. It is a bearing, not an observation: nothing here can see what is there.
      {%- endif %}
    </p>
  </section>

  {% if case.evidence %}
  <section>
    <h2>What the report shows</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Classification</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.evidence.pollution_type.value.replace("_", " ") }}</dd>
      <dt>Severity</dt><dd>{{ case.evidence.severity }}</dd>
      <dt>Confidence</dt><dd>{{ "%.2f"|format(case.evidence.confidence) }}</dd>
    </dl>
    {% if case.evidence.visible_indicators %}
    <h3>Indicators</h3>
    <ul>{% for item in case.evidence.visible_indicators %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if case.evidence.landmarks %}
    <h3>Landmarks recorded</h3>
    <ul>{% for item in case.evidence.landmarks %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if case.evidence.reasoning %}
    <h3>Reasoning</h3>
    <p class="prose">{{ case.evidence.reasoning }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if case.corroboration %}
  <section>
    <h2>Independent evidence</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        {% if case.corroboration.corroborated %}
          Corroborated by an independent sensor.
        {% else %}
          Not corroborated by an independent sensor.
        {% endif %}
      </strong>
      {% if not case.corroboration.corroborated %}
      An absence of detections is usually an absence of coverage rather than an absence of
      the event: hyper-local pollution routinely escapes satellites and distant stations.
      {% endif %}
    </p>
    <dl class="facts">
      {% if case.corroboration.satellite_summary %}
      <dt>Satellite</dt><dd>{{ case.corroboration.satellite_summary }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Thermal detections</dt><dd>{{ case.corroboration.satellite_fire_detections }}</dd>
      {% if case.corroboration.air_quality_summary %}
      <dt>Ground stations</dt><dd>{{ case.corroboration.air_quality_summary }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.corroboration.nearest_station_km is not none %}
      <dt>Nearest station</dt>
      <dd>{{ "%.1f"|format(case.corroboration.nearest_station_km) }} km</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.corroboration.dominant_pollutant %}
      <dt>Dominant pollutant</dt><dd>{{ case.corroboration.dominant_pollutant }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.corroboration.wind_speed_ms is not none %}
      <dt>Wind</dt>
      <dd>{{ case.corroboration.wind_speed_ms }} m/s
          {% if case.corroboration.wind_from_degrees is not none %}
          from {{ case.corroboration.wind_from_degrees }}&deg;{% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if case.corroboration.upwind_source_latitude is not none %}
      <dt>Back-traced point</dt>
      <dd>{{ "%.5f"|format(case.corroboration.upwind_source_latitude) }},
          {{ "%.5f"|format(case.corroboration.upwind_source_longitude) }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
    {% if case.corroboration.corroboration_notes %}
    <h3>Notes</h3>
    <p class="prose">{{ case.corroboration.corroboration_notes }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if cluster %}
  <section>
    <h2>Pattern of repeat reports</h2>
    <p>{{ pattern_sentence }}</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Reference</dt><dd>{{ cluster.cluster_id }}</dd>
      <dt>Reports</dt><dd>{{ cluster.report_count }}</dd>
      <dt>First reported</dt><dd>{{ cluster.first_reported_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      <dt>Most recent</dt><dd>{{ cluster.last_reported_at.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</dd>
      <dt>Identified reporters</dt><dd>{{ cluster.distinct_reporters }}</dd>
      <dt>Anonymous submissions</dt><dd>{{ cluster.anonymous_reports }}</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Anonymous submissions may be one person or many; nothing stored can tell, so they are
      counted apart rather than assumed independent.
    </p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if case.jurisdiction %}
  <section>
    <h2>Jurisdiction</h2>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Authority</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.authority_name }}</dd>
      <dt>Tier</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.authority_tier }}</dd>
      {% if case.jurisdiction.office %}
      <dt>Office</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.office }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Statute</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.statute }}</dd>
      {% if case.jurisdiction.section %}
      <dt>Section</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.section }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Response window</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.response_window_days }} days</dd>
      {% if case.jurisdiction.escalation_authority %}
      <dt>Escalates to</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.escalation_authority }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Match quality</dt><dd>{{ case.jurisdiction.coverage }}</dd>
    </dl>
    {% if case.jurisdiction.coverage != "exact" %}
    <p class="note">
      This authority was not an exact entry in the jurisdiction table.
      {{ case.jurisdiction.coverage_note or
         "Confirm the correct office before relying on this addressee." }}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if case.complaint %}
  <section>
    <h2>The complaint</h2>
    <h3>{{ case.complaint.subject }}</h3>
    <p class="prose">{{ case.complaint.body_en }}</p>
    {% if case.complaint.requested_action %}
    <h3>Action requested</h3>
    <p class="prose">{{ case.complaint.requested_action }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if case.complaint.cited_statutes %}
    <h3>Statutes cited</h3>
    <ul>{% for item in case.complaint.cited_statutes %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  {% if case.complaint.body_local %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ case.complaint.local_language or "Local language" }}</h2>
    <p class="local">{{ case.complaint.body_local }}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if case.rti %}
  <section>
    <h2>Right to Information application</h2>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Drafted for the citizen to complete and file in their own name. Nothing has been sent.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">{{ case.rti.body_en }}</p>
    {% if case.rti.placeholders %}
    <h3>To be filled in before filing</h3>
    <ul>{% for item in case.rti.placeholders %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if case.rti.body_local %}
    <h3>{{ case.rti.local_language or "Local language" }}</h3>
    <p class="local">{{ case.rti.body_local }}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% elif rti_available %}
  <section>
    <h2>Right to Information</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The statutory window has lapsed without an answer, so a Right to Information
      application asking what action was taken can now be drafted for this case. None has
      been yet.
    </p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if case.history %}
  <section>
    <h2>Timeline</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      {% for entry in case.history %}
      {% set stamp, _, text = entry.partition(" ") %}
      <li><time>{{ stamp[:16].replace("T", " ") }}</time>{{ text }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <footer>
    <p>
      <strong>How this document was produced.</strong> Every classification, corroboration
      summary and drafted paragraph above was written by a language model from the citizen's
      submission and from public data sources. It is a prepared complaint, not a finding of
      fact, and it names no responsible party.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Nothing here was delivered to a regulator by this system.</strong>
      {% if live_filing %}
      Live filing is switched on in this deployment's configuration, but no delivery
      transport exists in this software, so filing raises rather than sends.
      {% else %}
      Filing writes the complaint to a local sandbox outbox. The authority addresses this
      instance holds are reserved, non-routable placeholders.
      {% endif %}
      Sending this to the authority named above is a decision for the citizen.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Reporter contact is withheld.</strong> The contact the citizen gave is held on
      the case and deliberately kept out of this document, which is written to be shared.
      Add it to the copy you send if you want a reply.
    </p>
    <p>Case {{ case.case_id }}{% if cluster %} &middot; pattern {{ cluster.cluster_id }}
      {%- endif %} &middot; compiled by Vayudoot on
      {{ generated_at.strftime("%d %B %Y at %H:%M UTC") }}.</p>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
